# 🚀 DevOpsified Go Web Application

## 📌 Project Overview

This project demonstrates how a simple **Golang web application** can be transformed into a production-oriented, DevOps-enabled application using modern **containerization, Kubernetes, CI/CD, Helm, AWS EKS, and GitOps** practices.

The original Go application was a basic web application serving web pages using Go's `net/http` package. I progressively integrated DevOps practices around the application to make it **containerized, scalable, automated, secure, and deployable on Kubernetes**.

The project follows an end-to-end workflow:

```text
Go Application
      ↓
Docker Containerization
      ↓
Docker Image
      ↓
Docker Hub
      ↓
Kubernetes Deployment
      ↓
Helm Chart
      ↓
AWS EKS
      ↓
GitHub Actions CI
      ↓
Argo CD GitOps CD
      ↓
Automated Kubernetes Deployment
```

