# 🔟 Deployed the Application to Amazon EKS

After testing the Kubernetes deployment, I deployed the application to **Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (EKS)**.

The architecture became:

```text
                    AWS
                     │
                     ▼
               Amazon EKS
                     │
             ┌───────┴───────┐
             ▼               ▼
          Node 1           Node 2
             │               │
             ▼               ▼
           Pods             Pods
```

I connected my local Kubernetes client to the EKS cluster using:

```bash
aws eks update-kubeconfig \
  --region eu-north-1 \
  --name Cluster-1
```

Then verified the cluster:

```bash
kubectl get nodes
```

And deployed the application using Helm:

```bash
helm install go-web-app ./go-web-app
```

