# 1️⃣2️⃣ Added Container Security Scanning

I integrated container security practices into the workflow using tools such as:

### Trivy

Used to scan container images for known vulnerabilities.

Example:

```bash
trivy image afsarsohail/afsar-go-web-app:latest
```

### Docker Scout

Used to analyze container images and identify vulnerabilities and security recommendations.

```bash
docker scout cves afsarsohail/afsar-go-web-app:latest
```

The purpose was to identify security issues before deploying the image to Kubernetes.

---

# 1️⃣3️⃣ Implemented GitOps With Argo CD

For continuous delivery, I used **Argo CD**.

Instead of manually deploying every new version to Kubernetes, Argo CD continuously monitors the desired state stored in Git.

The workflow became:

```text
Developer
    ↓
Git Push
    ↓
GitHub Actions
    ↓
Build + Test + Scan
    ↓
Docker Image
    ↓
Docker Hub
    ↓
Git Repository
    ↓
Argo CD
    ↓
AWS EKS
```

Argo CD follows the Git repository as the source of truth for the Kubernetes application's desired state.

If the Kubernetes cluster differs from the desired configuration, Argo CD can detect the drift and synchronize the application according to its configured policy.

